.TH SDL_HINT_OPENGL_ES_DRIVER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_OPENGL_ES_DRIVER \- A variable controlling what driver to use for OpenGL ES contexts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_OPENGL_ES_DRIVER \(dqSDL_OPENGL_ES_DRIVER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
On some platforms, currently Windows and X11, OpenGL drivers may support creating contexts with an OpenGL ES profile\[char46] By default SDL uses these profiles, when available, otherwise it attempts to load an OpenGL ES library, e\[char46]g\[char46] that provided by the ANGLE project\[char46] This variable controls whether SDL follows this default behaviour or will always load an OpenGL ES library\[char46]
.PP
Circumstances where this is useful include:
.PP

\(bu Testing an app with a particular OpenGL ES implementation, e\[char46]g ANGLE, or emulator, e\[char46]g\[char46] those from ARM, Imagination or Qualcomm\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Resolving OpenGL ES function addresses at link time by linking with the OpenGL ES library instead of querying them at run time with
.BR SDL_GL_GetProcAddress ()\[char46]
.PP
Caution: for an application to work with the default behaviour across different OpenGL drivers it must query the OpenGL ES function addresses at run time using
.BR SDL_GL_GetProcAddress ()\[char46]
.PP
This variable is ignored on most platforms because OpenGL ES is native or not supported\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Use ES profile of OpenGL, if available\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Load OpenGL ES library using the default library names\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before SDL is initialized\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

